# Example and debug directories
example.dir

# NeuroPress example harnesses (issue #693). Kept on disk for local runs but
# out of the branch: they are development and parity tooling, not part of the
# integration. Their CMake entry points were removed with them, so a checkout
# without these directories still configures.
context-transfer-engine/adapter/hdf5_vol/example/
# Everything under compressor/example/ EXCEPT the Gray-Scott HDF5 demo, which
# is the deployment-shaped example (no Clio code in the application) and the
# one people are pointed at -- it should not live only on one machine. The
# example CMakeLists guards each entry point on the files it needs, so a
# checkout with just the demo still configures.
context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/*
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/CMakeLists.txt
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_grayscott_h5/
# Same reasoning for the LAMMPS demo: a stock, unmodified simulation whose
# binary links nothing from Clio. Scripts and an input deck only -- CMake
# builds nothing here, the harness drives a prebuilt LAMMPS.
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_lammps_h5/
# And for the LAMMPS-as-a-library example: the third shape (liblammps linked
# in, Clio hosted in the same process, no HDF5). Its CMakeLists skips itself
# when no LAMMPS build is found, so a checkout without one still configures.
# The store directories its scripts write are run output, not source.
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_lammps_lib/
context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_lammps_lib/store*/
# And the field-replay driver: it reads field dumps a simulation already wrote,
# which is the only shape available for codes with no library interface to
# embed (Nyx). Plain C++ against the Clio client, no simulation dependency.
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_field_replay/
# And the IN-SITU counterpart of that replay: one shared library a patched Nyx
# dlopens from its own in-situ callback to hand over AMReX device pointers.
# Nothing here depends on Nyx or AMReX -- the ABI is plain C -- so it builds
# wherever the compressor does. The store directories its scripts write are run
# output, not source.
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_nyx_insitu/
context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_nyx_insitu/store*/

# And the same shape for VPIC: one shared library a vpic-kokkos DECK links and
# calls from begin_diagnostics. The deck is ours (paper-benchmark/vpic), so no
# simulation patch exists here at all; the ABI is plain C and the library
# builds wherever the compressor does.
!context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_vpic_insitu/
context-transfer-engine/compressor/example/neuropress_vpic_insitu/store*/

# NeuroPress differential parity harnesses (issue #693). Same reasoning as the
# example directories above: they compile a second project's CUDA sources from
# a path outside this tree (CLIO_NEUROPRESS_SRC_DIR) and exist to compare the
# port against it, which is development tooling rather than part of the
# integration. Their CMakeLists skips the whole directory when that tree or
# nvcomp is absent, so a checkout without them still configures and still runs
# every non-parity test.
context-transport-primitives/test/unit/compress/model/parity/

# Parity/sweep CSV output, written into the working directory by the harnesses
# and examples above.
neuropress_*_parity.csv
neuropress_modes_parity.csv
neuropress_selection_parity.csv
Win32/
x64/
Release/
Debug/

